{
  "title": "Cleft Hand",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6072/cleft-hand",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cleft Hand is a congenital hand deformity caused by a defect in the central part of the apical ectodermal ridge during embryological development, that is characterized by the absence of 1 or more central digits of the hand or foot.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the absence or shortening of the central (third) ray with the absence of radial digits and/or syndactyly of the ulnar digits.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation versus reconstruction depending on the degree of functional limitation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**rare (1:10,000 to 1:90,000)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male:female ratio is 5:1 (more common in **male**)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "hands, usually bilateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated with **absent metacarpals** (helps differentiate from symbrachydactyly)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**missing middle finger**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**on the ulnar side, small finger** is always present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "often involves feet as well",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathogenesis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "theory is wedge-shaped degeneration of **central part of apical ectodermal ridge (AER)** because of loss of function of certain genes expressed in that part of the AER",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Types",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "unilateral vs bilateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "isolated vs syndromic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Forms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**typical** (central) cleft hand is characterized by",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "also known as lobster-claw deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Swanson type I failure of formation** (longitudinal arrest) of central ray, leaving **V-shaped cleft** in the center of the hand",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inheritance pattern",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**autosomal dominant** with reduced penetrance (70%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inherited forms become more severe with each generation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "mutations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "deletions, inversions, translocations of 7q",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "split hand-split foot syndrome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "affected families should undergo **genetic counseling**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Ectrodactyly-ectodermal dysplasia-cleft (EEC) syndrome**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sensorineural hearing loss",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "syndactyly and polydactyly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
